========================================================================================
LRC(14) colored resonance deficit scout
========================================================================================
Goal: replace raw K by a color-resonance/coarse-component discrepancy bound.

========================================================================================
STEP 1. Rigorous Fourier/color-resonance identity
========================================================================================
Let h(x)=1_{||x||>=1/14}, with boundary values taken as 1/2
for the Fourier identity.  For a fixed color b define
  F_b(x)=prod_{p in P} h(px) * prod_{e in E} h(ex-b/14).
The half-boundary colored count is
  N(P,E,V)=sum_b sum_{t=0}^{V-1} F_b(t/V+b/(14V)).
Writing Fourier coefficients in x, the grid quadrature gives
  N - V*Sigma = V * sum_{ell != 0} sum_b Fhat_b(ell V) exp(2pi i ell b/14).
Expanding each h-factor, a term can survive the color sum only if
  sum_p p*n_p + sum_e e*n_e = ell*V
  and  sum_e n_e == ell (mod 14).
This is the colored resonance condition.  Raw interval endpoints count
all micro-events; the actual discrepancy only sees these compatible
V-resonances.  The closed CRT count differs from the half-boundary
count by the explicit binding-boundary bonus, which the diagnostics print.

