========================================================================================
TAKEAWAY
========================================================================================
  1. The exact discrepancy is governed by a colored resonance condition,
     not by raw micro-component count K.
  2. Direct rows refute too-small constant bounds, but additive bounds
     C*(k+cGP)+1 are the right-looking next theorem target.
  3. A proof should bound the surviving Fourier/color resonances or,
     equivalently, prove endpoint cancellation inside each coarse G_P
     component after summing the 14 phase colors.
  4. This is still not a proof of LRC(14), but it is a precise lemma:
     colored discrepancy <= C*(k+cGP)+1 plus the Sigma floor would leave
     only a finite low-V exact check.
